## ⚙️ Multi-Block Validation Engine Design
To maintain the absolute zero-allocation constraints expected by your Sentinel kernel, the streaming validator operates on three runtime execution principles:
## 1. Zero-Copy Windowing

* The system never duplicates packet memory into intermediate buffers.
* The ingestion framework passes raw, unmanaged pointers (const uint8_t*) directly to downstream processing systems after checksum validation.

## 2. Strict Frame Invariant Check

* The validator evaluates total_len at byte offset 0x04 during every single iteration.
* If total_len drops below the absolute minimum frame size of 61 bytes, the engine halts immediately. This prevents malicious underflow attacks designed to trap the parsing pointer in an infinite processing loop.

## 3. Single-Pass Execution Alignment

* The loop computes the XOR parity check dynamically alongside the streaming boundary assertions.
* This approach keeps data localized inside L1 processor caches, preventing memory bus degradation during heavy database imports.

